            <ArticleTitle>Eighty-two year old female with long term abdominal pain, fever and skin lesions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>285-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.rce.2014.06.016</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0014-2565(14)00298-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of an old woman, consulting for fever, abdominal pain and constitutional symptoms one year of evolution. The differential diagnosis is between infectious, tumoral, or inflammatory disease, which may be located at the abdominal level, performing additional tests to rule out abdominal process. The existence of pain in the legs and level scan left thigh of a mass of hard consistency, makes us raise another diagnosis. Finally show on ultrasound soft tissue inflammatory changes regarding panniculitis. From this finding aetiologies of panniculitis are reviewed. Skin biopsy that shows the final diagnosis is made.</AbstractText>
